  "title": "Adult Post-Resuscitation Care & Checklist",
  "markdown": "# Adult Post-Resuscitation Care & Checklist\n\n![Visual reference from Adult Post-Resuscitation Care & Checklist](../../assets/figures/page-0054-visual.webp)\n\n| | SAVE A LIFE |\n|---|---|\n| S | **S**tabilize - Stay on scene vs. rapid departure |\n| A | **A**irway - if still unresponsive, establish a definitive airway (SGA, ETT) |\n| V | **V**itals - change frequency to every 3 minutes<br>**V**asopressors (NOREPInephrine) - focus on cerebral perfusion pressure, goal is MAP greater than 80 mmHg |\n| E | **E**tCO2 - monitor airway and for re-arrest |\n| A | **A**lert/activate hospital |\n| L | **L**eave/**L**oad in ambulance with mechanical CPR device in place, if available in case patient rearrests en route to hospital |\n| I | **I**V - if only an IO has been placed |\n| F | **F**ollow-up vital signs to ensure stability before departure |\n| E | **E**CG - may affect destination, delayed ECG increases accuracy |\n",
  "plain_text": "Adult Post-Resuscitation Care & Checklist SAVE A LIFE S Stabilize - Stay on scene vs. rapid departure A Airway - if still unresponsive, establish a definitive airway (SGA, ETT) V Vitals - change frequency to every 3 minutes Vasopressors (NOREPInephrine) - focus on cerebral perfusion pressure, goal is MAP greater than 80 mmHg E EtCO2 - monitor airway and for re-arrest A Alert/activate hospital L Leave/Load in ambulance with mechanical CPR device in place, if available in case patient rearrests en route to hospital I IV - if only an IO has been placed F Follow-up vital signs to ensure stability before departure E ECG - may affect destination, delayed ECG increases accuracy",
