      "text": "Adult Post-Resuscitation Car e Checklist\nSAVE A LIFE\nS Stabilize - Stay on scene vs. rapid departure\nA Airway - if still unresponsive, establish a definitive airway (SGA, ETT)\nVitals - change frequency to every 3 minutes\nV V\nasopressors (NOREPInephrine) - focus on cerebral perfusion\npressure, goal is MAP greater than 80 mmHg\nE EtCO - monitor airway and for re-arrest\n2\nA Alert/activate hospital\nLeave/Load in ambulance with mechanical CPR device in place, if\nL\navailable in case patient rearrests en route to hospital\nI IV - if only an IO has been placed\nF Follow-up vital signs to ensure stability before departure\nE ECG - may affect destination, delayed ECG increases accuracy\n(Back to TOC) Red 17",
